Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:12:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] async GRPO: optionally skip prompt groups with zero
 advantage

grpo.skip_zero_advantage_groups leaves groups whose rewards are all equal
out of the logprob and training passes; they add nothing to the policy
gradient. The trained rows are padded with the shortest skipped rows to a
multiple of optimizer steps x data-parallel ranks, and their advantages
are scaled by the kept share of loss tokens so each optimizer step equals
the full-batch one. On DAPO-Math this trains about 2/3 of the rows.
